okay so invincible was by far one of the  best superhero shows of last year at a  time when disney are often accused of  playing their mcu shows too safe  invincible came along and completely  knocked it out the park the series was  filled with over-the-top gore amazing  action scenes and also several twists  and turns throughout that made it a must  watch at the heart of it was omniman  who's arguably the most memorable aspect  of the entire show but why is he the  perfect villain for the amazon series  well throughout this video that's what  we're going to be going over now because  of this there will be some spoilers so  if you haven't had a chance to check out  the full series then i highly recommend  that you check out now if you agree with  us then please hit the thumbs up button  and also don't forget to subscribe for  videos like this every day without the  way thank you for clicking this now  let's get into why omniman is the  perfect villain  okay so invincible episode 1 introduced  us to the titular character and his  father omniman superheroes are a dime a  dozen at this point and if you weren't  familiar with the source material then  you might think that this was just  another carbon copy of superman  throughout the initial entry we watched  as mark came to grips with his powers  and also learned some of his father's  origin story you would tell that he was  a protector of peace and justice who  came from the planet veltrum this planet  was supposed to be not too dissimilar to  our own but those that lived there had  abilities far beyond what we have  omniman tells mark that belgium was  somewhat a utopia that had achieved  perfection through taking no tolerance  towards murder and war with no conflict  to tackle the high council decree that  their society shouldn't become  complacent and they sent their people  out into the stars in order to help the  universe achieve the perfection that  they had omniman or rather nolan as he  calls himself says that he and several  scientists travel through the cosmos  improving planets and the life forms on  them he was apparently given the job of  helping earth and it became his second  home after he met a woman named debbie  the pair settled down had a kid and he's  protected the planet ever since now  though he looks like henry cavill in  justice league before the vfx work the  two couldn't be more dissimilar and we  learn that this is actually a lie come  the season finale or issue 11 in the  comics we learn the truth and it goes  down worse than joss whedon at a  feminist rally that's two joss whedon  jokes back to back  now this is one of the major things that  makes omniman so fascinating we live in  a society where people are often propped  up as heroes however over time we learn  that the truth is far more shadowy than  that and they often aren't all they  appear to be i think the song says sojo  by murray head sums this up perfectly  and it's become somewhat of a cultural  icon written in the 70s prior to richard  nixon's resignation the tune was based  on a documentary in which a presenter  asked people in a small town what they  thought about the president even in the  face of conclusive evidence and proof  they still showed their support and this  was further likened to the story of joe  jackson whose name appears in the title  of the song during the 1920s joe was a  baseball player that reportedly took a  bribe to lose the final of the world  series and people at the stadium chanted  say it ain't so joe our heroes are our  heroes and sometimes it's difficult to  see them any other way even if they're  shown not to be i think that omniman  perfectly symbolizes this and come the  end of the first episode i saw people  who are unaware of the twist still  rallying for him in the post-credits  scene of episode 1 we watch him brutally  massacre the guardians of the globe and  upon its release many people believe  that this was mind control a clone or  something else they did anything to save  the hero and all that he stood for come  episode 8 though we learned the truth  and mark very much has this reaction too  he can't believe his dad's like this and  speaking from personal experience it's  difficult for us to see the flaws in our  parents even when they do bad i'd say  it's way easier to forgive them than it  is to forgive a friend and this is very  much cemented in the pairs exchange  throughout the finale we learn what  belgium really stands for and that it  actually forced its population to fight  one another in order to weed out the  weak they killed fifty percent of all  velcro mites and all that was left when  they just settled was the best of the  best of the best sir the high council  then decided to send out the world  conquering committee and due to their  enhanced strength they took over several  civilizations in order to build an  empire those that surrendered became  enslaved and their planets were picked  dry of all their resources those that  resisted were wiped out and the veltrome  empire spanned the galaxy however over  time their forces were spread too thin  and thus they had to devise a new plan  rather than just attacking planets  they'd send in a trojan horse who'd take  the form of a hero our great villains  are always great because you can see the  positive aspects of their plans nolan  doesn't really see himself as the bad  guy and he also discusses the benefits  that come with earth joining the empire  though they'd picked the planet clean  this would take thousands and thousands  of years and in that time humanity would  prosper beltram would give us the  advanced medical care that they  developed they'd end war on the planet  and everyone on earth would live in  peace and harmony until we became  extinct which sounds nice i guess now  you can definitely see the benefits of  it and nolan in his mind was very much  doing right by us and right by his own  people he started to slip into society  and he picked a pet and deborah who he  decided to raise his son with because  voltron my dna is so pure it completely  overruled the human aspects of him and  mark gained all the abilities that his  dad has nolan's plan was to raise him to  become as merciless as he was but  humanity had other ideas and that kind  of takes us to the battle between the  pair which spans the planet it's bloody  brutal has thousands of deaths in it and  it's clear that nolan completely  outmatches his son there's some  absolutely unforgettable moments in the  episode such as when mark saves a pilot  and then omniman crushes his head just  to show how insignificant we are he also  forces his son's face through a train  and yeah hard to get this image out your  head now omniman's just impossible to be  on a physical level but what the series  does perfectly is that it allows him to  be defeated on an emotional one  throughout the entry nolan explains that  his vulture might get older they age  more slowly and that mark's lifespan  will last for thousands and thousands of  years after pummeling his son to an inch  of his life nolan asks his son what  he'll have in thousands of years when  everything is gone and he says he'll  have him it completely breaks nolan and  we get a flashback to a time when he  likely first saw the good in humanity  watching the smile on his son's face as  he plays baseball makes him see him as a  person instead of an object of war and  it completely breaks the character  throughout his entire life he's been  told that having emotions is weak and  that the weak must perish however for  once he sees things from another point  of view and this completely changes his  perspective villains like the best  heroes are often that way because  they're flawed and we can see in them  aspects of ourselves i'm sure many of us  growing up have got caught up in an  ideal and because of this we've been  jerks to people who don't agree with  what we think is right whether it's  religion lifestyle choices or just  general attitudes we can often end up  seeing things only in black and white  which ultimately leads to our values  being questioned sometimes we agree with  a counter-argument and change and often  this is for the better this is what  nolan very much represents and why he's  the perfect villain he has a stance and  takes it but he can also become weakened  in that viewpoint when the right thing  is presented to him however that doesn't  mean he changes completely and nolan  flies off into space leaving a single  teardrop behind he's clearly broken and  if you've read the comics then you'll  know the arc of redemption that he  somewhat goes on i don't want to spoil  it as i know you guys might still want  some surprises but omniman is the  perfect villain because of the change  that we see in him he's very much a  father figure that is set in his ways  but after he sees the good in his  children he decides to change it's  something that's been seen in darth  vader and it's a motif that works over  and over again because it's always based  on emotions rather than physical  strength omniman is one of the most  memorable superheroes to come out in the  last 20 years or so and he perfectly  deconstructs what it would be like to  have the power of a god that only deals  in absolutes he's questioned and then  changes and this very much makes us  wonder if we would be strong enough to  change our minds if we could do whatever  we wanted because of these reasons  omniman is fascinating and looking back  at invincible he's the perfect villain i  hope you enjoyed the video and i'd of  course love to hear your thoughts so  make sure you comment below and let me  know we're on a competition right now  and giving away three copies of the june  box on the 28th of feb and all you have  to do to be on the chance of winning is  like the video make sure you subscribe  with notifications on and drop a comment  below with your thoughts on the video we  picked the comments at random at the end  of the month and the winners of the last  one are on screen right now so if that's  you then message me on twitter at  heavyspoilers if you want some else to  watch then make sure you check out one  of our videos on screen right now  especially the perfect scene playlist we  talk about lots of things that we love  it's very positive very uplifting we  don't like to moan that much so  hopefully it'll cheer you up and make  your day a bit better without the way  thanks for sitting through the video  i've been paul let's see on the next one  take care peace

